s nasty remarks about colleagues is also severe. So both have interpersonal issues. Which is worse? Nasty remarks likely more disruptive. So C may be better overall.\n\nThus we can support C, but note concerns and suggest maybe we need to address communication training. So we vote for C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's point. Provide evidence: \"C can make correct decisions quickly\" and \"C keeps calm in a crisis\" (stress resilience). Also mention \"C is regarded as egocentric\" as a concern but outweighed.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nLet's craft."}
